# x-residual-moves-b-client: desktop wiring (DESKTOP-WIRE-G10)

The handlers in ipc-projects.ts, ipc-file-dialogs.ts, ipc-source-control.ts and ipc-sessions.ts (committed with this task) take an optional
`core` option: this PC's core connection. Until the hot files below pass it they fail with "The core connection is not available." (no
other implementation is kept). Everything below was applied to a scratch copy, type-checked (npx tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.node.json and
-p tsconfig.web.json clean) and its tests run before it was taken out again.

## 1. ipc.ts and index.ts (hot files): apply this patch (git apply, paths from the repository root)

- ipc.ts: `const localCore = pcCore ?? protocol ?? null;` passed as `core` to registerFileDialogIpc, registerProjectIpc and
  registerSourceControlIpc; `requestLinuxInputAccess` is the core's `desktop/computer/inputAccess/request` (linux-input-access.ts import gone).
- index.ts: the pet's `decideApproval` calls `localService.resolveToolApprovalForSession` directly (the core announces the `permissions`
  change itself, approval_notification.rs); the TypeScript network watcher is gone (the core's NetworkWatcher, composed in
  compose_domains/rows.rs, redials the relay leg: both would redial twice); the native tool cache gc is the core's
  `desktop/nativeToolCache/gc`, sent once the local protocol connection exists (`bundledNativeToolKinds` replaces the local `bundledKinds`);
  the unused `net` and `homedir` imports go.

