## 2. Delete after the patch (their last importers are the hunks above)

- apps/desktop/src/main/approval-grant-change.ts
- apps/desktop/src/main/native-runtime-cache-gc.mjs, native-runtime-cache-gc.d.mts, native-runtime-cache-gc.test.mjs
- apps/desktop/src/main/network-watch.ts, network-watch.test.mjs
- apps/desktop/src/main/linux-input-access.ts, linux-input-access.test.mjs

Each test case maps to a Rust test in native/core/crates/mixdog-core-domains/src/domains/desktop_residual_b_tests.rs
(a_superseded_native_cache_is_removed_and_the_others_stay; the_network_signature_lists_external_addresses_in_order,
the_leg_redials_when_the_network_returns_or_changes_while_online, the_watcher_fires_on_a_change_and_stops,
an_interface_that_joins_without_a_route_change_is_a_network_change; the_uinput_rule_is_installed_once_and_only_when_needed,
two_requests_in_flight_share_one_prompt, the_privileged_script_holds_constants_only) and to desktop_residual_b.rs. approval-grant-change.ts has
no test: approval_notification_tests.rs (the answer that stored a standing grant announces `permissions` once).

## 3. shared/core-lanes/blob-ref-fields.ts (with the core fragment x-residual-moves-b-client.wire, blob_fields.json)

The two data-carrying methods are sent as blobs (core-blob-ref.ts). Add to BLOB_REF_FIELDS, in the same place as blob_fields.json
(sized-call.test.mjs asserts the two tables are equal):

    'desktop/attachment/write': ['/dataUrl'],
    'desktop/userFile/write': ['/dataBase64'],

## 4. Stays, with the reason (not deleted by this task)

- launch-version.ts, model-bootstrap.ts: they run before the core connection exists and gate the first window (`await launchFollowsUpdate`
  before createMainBrowserWindow) and the first snapshot (`initialSnapshot`, a synchronous read at construction). Their core methods
  (`desktop/launchVersion/record|acknowledge`, `desktop/modelBootstrap/read`) are registered; calling them there would put the daemon's start
  on the window's critical path. A caller that has a connection is a change of that boot order, which this task does not make.
- login-shell-environment.ts: the core now reads the login shell itself at the start of `run()` (mixdog-app-server-daemon lib.rs), so a
  desktop launch reads it twice (the TypeScript read first, then the core's). The TypeScript read stays only because the Electron main
  process's own children (ssh, the notification sound player, the browser profile import, the Linux helpers) inherit `process.env`, and no
  core method hands the adopted variables back to the desktop. Closing it needs a method (for example `desktop/loginShell/environment`
  answering `LoginShellAdoption.set`) that main applies to its own environment once connected; then this file, its test and the
  index.ts block go. Lead decision (a protocol row and a core line).
- session-sidebar-actions.ts, ipc-control-chars.ts, git-contract.mjs, child-environment.ts: their rows are in Rust (mixdog-core-session,
  the boundary validators, mixdog-tools exec env), and their only importers are IPC files that s2a-del-ipc-handlers, s2a-del-validation and
  s1-del-terminal delete (ipc-sessions.ts, ipc-validation.ts, ipc-source-control.ts, terminal-manager.ts); they go with those.
